  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "🦎 Argonian Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Jel-style names like Jaree-Ra, or descriptive names like Scouts-Many-Marshes."
    },
    "intro": "Argonians have two kinds of name. Some sound like their own language, Jel: Jaree-Ra, Keerava, Derkeethus. Others are descriptions in plain words, joined with hyphens: Scouts-Many-Marshes on the Windhelm docks is the classic example. This **Argonian name generator** gives you both, for Skyrim, Elder Scrolls Online or your own trip to Black Marsh.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Two kinds of Argonian name",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Jel-style names</strong> come from the Argonians' own language. They're short, with doubled vowels (ee, aa), hyphens and sounds like j, sh and x: Jaree-Ra and his sister Deeja, Keerava who runs the Bee and Barb in Riften, Talen-Jei who works there, and Derkeethus, rescued from Darkwater Pass.</li><li><strong>Descriptive names</strong> are translations: a few hyphenated words describing the Argonian, or something they do. Scouts-Many-Marshes and Neetrenaza both work on Windhelm's docks; only one has a name you can read.</li></ul><p>An Argonian may use either, or both, depending on who they're talking to.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Black Marsh and the Hist",
        "content": "<p>Argonians come from Black Marsh, the swampland in the south-east of Tamriel. Their lives are bound to the Hist, the great sentient trees of the marsh; hatchlings lick the sap of the Hist, which shapes who they become.</p><p>That's one reason descriptive names suit Argonians so well. A name like Listens-To-Hist or Knows-Many-Roots puts the swamp and the trees right in the name.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Choosing a name",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Descriptive names make a great hook.</strong> Someone will always ask why a character is called Bites-Twice.</li><li><strong>Jel names suit Argonians who keep to their own kind,</strong> or who don't care whether outsiders can say their name.</li><li><strong>Use both.</strong> Give your Argonian a Jel name at home and a descriptive name among the other races.</li></ul><p>For other races of Tamriel, see the <a href=\"khajiit-name-generator.html\">Khajiit</a>, <a href=\"dunmer-name-generator.html\">Dunmer</a> and <a href=\"nord-name-generator.html\">Nord</a> name generators.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "Why do some Argonians have names like Scouts-Many-Marshes?",
        "answer": "They're descriptive names: plain words describing the Argonian or something they do, joined with hyphens. Others use names from their own language, Jel, like Jaree-Ra."
      },
      {
        "question": "Are Argonian names gendered?",
        "answer": "Not in any obvious way, so the generator doesn't split them. Use any name for any Argonian."
      },
      {
        "question": "Are these names from Skyrim?",
        "answer": "No. They're new names in the same two styles, so your character won't share one with someone in the game."
      }
    ]
  }
